    "https://games.crossfit.com/leaderboard/games/2010",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_CrossFit_Games",
    "https://www.crossfit.com/workout/2010/07/23",
    "Scoring is placement-equals-points; ranks and points are taken directly from the official c3po leaderboard archive and reconcile exactly to each athlete's overall score. Score displays are the official leaderboard values normalized ('rep' -> 'reps'). For the three-part Sunday final, leaderboard rep figures for athletes who FINISHED an event are encoded values (reps plus an unpublished time-remaining bonus), not literal reps, per the raw anchor file. For those events the place-1 winner's score uses the documented finishing time (Event 2010-07 men Froning 6:55; Event 2010-09 men Spealler 8:32; Event 2010-09 women Thorisdottir 7:34). Patrick Burke's Event 2010-09 finish (10:41) is documented and used; other finishers' encoded rep artifacts with no published time are set to null. Capped athletes' literal rep counts are kept as shown."
